 | `TF_GLM_OVN_PIECE_MLA` | Exactly `0` or `1`; default off (as `TF_GLM_OVN_PIECE_FRONT`, for an ffn site that a DSA layer follows: the layer's projections, norms, indexer and absorbed query run piece by piece; the bits are the same) |
 | `TF_GLM_OVN_FRONT_ROWS` | Whole number; with `TF_GLM_OVN_PIECE_FRONT`, `_MLA` or `_FFN` a front range joins pieces until it has at least this many rows (fewer weight reads on a small chunk, the bits the same); default 0 (a range a piece) |
 | `TF_GLM_OVN_PIECE_KDA` | Exactly `0` or `1`; default off (a prompt chunk's KDA mixer site runs its chain piece by piece, each range of rows ahead of its pieces' o_proj and exchange, instead of the whole chain before the first piece; the bits are the same) |
+| `TF_GLM_OVN_SOLO_TO_START` | Exactly `0` or `1`; default off (with `TF_GLM_CHUNK_SOLO=4096` and `TF_GLM_REQUEST_STARTS=1`, a solo prompt step whose second chunk holds a request start ends at that start instead of being refused, so the stretch before a message start runs as one pass and not two; the tokens are the same) |
 | `TF_GLM_OVN_KDA_CHUNKED` | Exactly `0` or `1`; default off (prompt chunks' KDA chain on production's chunked (WY) kernel; replies are not the serial chain's bit for bit) |
 | `TF_GLM_OVN_MM_WIDE` | Whole number; set, prompt linears take glm_mm's 128 x 128 blocks in L2 row bands (2: 32 x 32 warps, any other: 64 x 32); default 0 (off) |
 | `TF_GLM_OVN_MM_CLUSTER` | Whole count of Mi values; weights at least this large sum a decode tile's K slices in a cluster; default 0 (off) |
